/*
 * A BARE `npx tsc --noEmit` IN THIS DIRECTORY CHECKS NOTHING. `files` is empty and the real
 * configs hang off `references`, which only `tsc -b` (project-build mode) follows — so the bare
 * command exits 0 on a file with `const x: number = 'nope'` in it. That is not hypothetical: it is
 * how a genuinely broken admin build could pass typechecking unnoticed: keep the admin build
 * and source contract checks in the required project-build path.
 *
 * The real gates are `npm run typecheck` (`tsc -b`) and `npm run build` (`tsc -b && vite build`).
 * Use those.
 */
{
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "./tsconfig.app.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.node.json" }
  ]
}
